WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.030
Ron! 5,200.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.700
Himematsu's Suehara

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.220
immediately plays into Miyamori's 
Anetai's chasing riichi!

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:15.670
Riichi, ippatsu, one dora: 
that will cost her 5,200 points.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.630
And that's it for the first half!

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.090
<i>Her chasing riichi beat me again.</i>

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.450
<i>This is just too...</i>

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:51.030
<b>The Nationals</b>

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:10.790
<b>Hand 10: 
Friends</b>

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:10.350
We've had our break, and now 
it's time for the second half.

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:14.770
Himematsu's Suehara, who started in first,

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:17.360
had a great opening with three consecutive wins,

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.620
but after having to make a payment and

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.190
playing into other players' hands four times,

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:24.490
she has lost 21,600 points in the first half.

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:28.370
She is only 900 points ahead 
of second place Kiyosumi.

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:34.190
<i>This isn't good.</i>

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.380
<i>I've got to rethink my strategy.</i>

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.940
Kiyosumi's Miyanaga remains in second,

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:46.470
where she started, gaining 
5,500 points in the first half.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:50.370
However, Himematsu's first
place is well within reach.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.480
We can expect an exciting second half!

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:58.280
Moving from last to third is Miyamori's Anetai.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:01.110
She raked in 12,100 points,
the highest gain in the first half.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:03.950
In the second half, she'll be 
aiming for a top two position,

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.940
qualifying her team for the semifinals.

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:10.910
It's stopped raining.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:16.190
Sae will be okay, probably.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.590
That's good!

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:20.510
I'll avenge her!

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:22.370
Yeah.

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:28.630
Nighttime in Tokyo is so pretty.

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:30.390
You can't see any stars, though.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:34.900
Yeah, but... all these lights 
look like a starry sky!

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:39.490
Toyone, are you having fun?

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:40.950
Huh?

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.080
I am!

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:46.870
I'm so glad I was able to 
come here with all of you.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:50.150
I'm going to do my best 
in the second half, too.

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:01.250
Falling from third to last place is,

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:02.880
surprisingly, the seed school, Eisui.

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:05.830
However, they had still gained 
points in the first half.

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:08.840
They'll be aiming for a 
comeback in the second half.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.990
How are you feeling?

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:25.450
Neither of us got a chance to 
play in the first round match.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.740
It's been a while since we 
played an official game.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.420
Yeah.

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:32.170
That's Nationals for you.

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:34.240
It doesn't always go as desired.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:38.090
Plus, I feel like someone's 
still hiding something.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:43.380
The second half will begin shortly.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:47.290
All participating players, 
please report to the stage.

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:47.890
It's almost time.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:50.100
All right. Here I go.

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:51.390
Okay!

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:56.150
Saki-san!

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:56.880
Huh?

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:00.800
Um...

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:04.650
Let's go to the semifinals together!

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:07.050
Yes.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:22.940
There's Saki-chan!

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:45.820
This will be the last East-South 
match in round two's third game!

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:50.320
Which schools will make it to the semifinals?

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:54.080
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
 3rd Year
 Anetai Toyone

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.830
Himematsu High School 
(South Osaka)
 3rd Year
 Suehara Kyouko

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:01.630
Kiyosumi High School 
(Nagano)
 1st Year
 Miyanaga Saki

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.340
Eisui Girls' (Kagoshima)
 3rd Year
 Iwato Kasumi

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:07.630
And the second half has begun!

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:17.540
Fifth Players' Match, Second Half

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:17.540
East Hand 1
 Dealer - Anetai Toyone

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:22.930
<i>If anyone declares a riichi, 
she'll chase them down,</i>

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:27.190
<i>but if nobody does, Anetai 
can't declare one herself.</i>

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:30.950
<i>Then we're on even footing.</i>

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:34.760
<i>No, I'm at an advantage because 
I can call tiles and declare riichi faster!</i>

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.830
<i>Anetai can't call any tiles!</i>

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:40.710
Pon!

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:45.910
<i>In order to make her chasing riichi work,</i>

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:48.040
<i>she must keep her hand closed...</i>

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.840
<i>Why did she just call?</i>

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:54.300
<i>Does she have something up her sleeve</i>

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.220
<i>besides her chasing riichi?</i>

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:58.730
Chi!

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:06.650
<i>This is probably still okay, right?</i>

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:08.900
Pon!

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.060
Chi!

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:21.920
<i>This is...</i>

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.740
<i>a naked wait!</i>

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:27.420
It's not alone!

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:29.880
It's East Hand 1 of the match's second half.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.550
Miyamori's Anetai

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:33.950
suddenly made four calls and 
is now in a naked wait!

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:35.140
Toyone!

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:36.660
Tomobiki?

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:36.660
[Tomobiki, from the calendar of lucky and 
unlucky days, written as "attract friends"]

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:39.430
So she's finally revealing that one?

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:42.440
<i>Sae's feeling better...</i>

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:46.630
<i>What is this?</i>

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:49.620
<i>Even if it's a bluff to prove 
she can do more than just</i>

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:51.290
<i>chase riichis, this is too risky!</i>

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:55.750
I wanted that to stay hidden until the finals,

00:07:56.560 --> 00:08:01.410
but against Kiyosumi, I guess 
we can't afford that luxury.

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:05.780
Here comes a friend!

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:08.610
Tsumo!

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:10.270
2,000 from all.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:12.760
<i>No way...</i>

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.660
That was Anetai, with a 
tsumo worth 2,000 from all!

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.380
This moves her into second place.

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:18.970
You did it, Toyone!

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:20.440
Wow!

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:23.710
<i>Toyone...</i>

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:28.140
<i>In the beginning, nobody even 
made a decent match for her.</i>

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:32.810
<i>Has it only been half a year since then?</i>

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:37.280
Half a Year Ago
 Miyamori Girls' 
High School

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:40.540
Ah!

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:41.790
I thought you'd be here!

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:45.030
Kosegawa-san! Want to go to the cafeteria?

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:49.270
I'm tired right now. Ask me some other time.

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:52.300
No dice again today? Too bad!

00:08:58.900 --> 00:08:59.810
Huh?

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:02.730
You're the exchange student.

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:06.180
I didn't know you sat behind me.

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:13.550
Growl

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:16.770
Are you... hungry?

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:17.820
Yeah.

00:09:18.310 --> 00:09:19.990
Want... some bread?

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:22.040
Yeah.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:29.540
Oh, there you are.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:30.450
Shiro!

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:33.610
Kumakura-sensei brought that 
girl she was talking about.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.880
I'm coming.

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:43.390
Thanks for the food.

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:53.180
Want to come, too?

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:55.860
Yes!

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:03.160
That took a while.

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:05.290
Sorry for the wait.

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:11.830
Can you introduce yourself?

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:13.590
Yes.

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:28.230
I'm from Iwate.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:30.210
My name is Anetai Toyone.

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:40.530
I'm from Iwate.

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:42.620
My name is Anetai Toyone.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.070
This is Iwate...

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:45.260
Wow, she's tall!

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:49.330
She's a second year student, 
just like you guys.

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:52.850
I was walking around taking a look 
at things before I came here.

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:56.030
That's when I found this outstanding talent.

00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:58.420
You should all play a game with her.

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:02.510
Good luck.

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:03.950
Good luck.

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:06.890
Thanks! Good luck!

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:09.160
This girl comes from a village

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:11.360
with very few young people.

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:14.870
Without a computer, 
she learned to play mahjong

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:18.780
by setting up the tiles herself 
and watching games on TV.

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:21.950
So does that mean you haven't 
played against others much?

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:23.450
Yeah.

00:11:23.840 --> 00:11:26.540
But she comes with my seal of approval.

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:30.080
That's pretty scary.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:32.290
Who's this girl?

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:35.280
This is Aislinn-san, the exchange student.

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:36.800
Pleased to meet you.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.780
Do you know how to play mahjong?

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:44.550
That's really too bad.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:46.980
Well, should we start?

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:48.060
Yeah!

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:51.110
Start with your Shakkou play.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:51.110
[Shakkou, from the calendar of lucky and 
unlucky days, written as "red mouth"]

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:52.060
Okay.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:37.980
Tsumo!

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:41.530
2,000 all.

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:44.030
It's over.

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:47.790
I can't win!

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:10.060
Why are you crying?!

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:15.850
I was having so much fun... 
and now I have to go home!

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:21.900
If I don't get on the next train, 
I won't make the last bus!

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:24.340
Oh, I see. That's too bad.

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:27.320
I couldn't win, but I still had a lot of fun.

00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:33.760
So...

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:34.500
Yeah?

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:37.250
When will you transfer here?

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:39.760
Huh?

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:42.640
We thought Kumakura-sensei

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:46.070
brought you here as a potential team member.

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:48.760
Are we wrong?

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:51.710
I... I didn't hear about that...

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:55.770
Well, I hadn't told anyone, but yes.

00:13:58.290 --> 00:14:01.980
I thought you'd never want someone like me

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:05.190
on your team... and... well...

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:07.240
We'd welcome you any time.

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:08.780
Yeah!

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:10.200
Yup!

00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:17.540
I've already gotten permission 
from the necessary parties,

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:19.960
and all the arrangements are made.

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:25.020
All that was left was seeing 
whether you all fit together.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:27.720
Whether... we all fit?

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:40.800
Huh?

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:42.900
Why are you crying again?!

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:48.820
I'm so happy!

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.430
Oh, that's all?

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:52.100
That surprised me!

00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:55.020
Don't scare us!

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:56.780
Yeah, really!

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:05.090
On paper, her transfer is already complete.

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:09.160
It has been since the time 
Toyone and I met, last fall.

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:10.010
Huh?

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:11.010
Oh!

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.510
That was an admission exam?

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:15.200
That's right.

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:19.400
Regional regulations made it 
difficult to get you here...

00:15:20.470 --> 00:15:22.020
But we finally did it.

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:24.890
So you've been making arrangements 
since fall last year.

00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:26.720
Why'd you start so long ago?

00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:27.730
Oh!

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:28.850
I see.

00:15:31.540 --> 00:15:34.700
You don't mean... the inter-high?!

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:37.700
Inter... high?

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:41.410
It's the national high 
school mahjong tournament!

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:43.720
They have it every summer!

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:45.500
Huh? So then... what?

00:15:46.030 --> 00:15:49.480
We've never played in a 
team tournament, either.

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:52.470
But don't you need five people for a team?

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:54.060
We're short one...

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:54.890
Me!

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:58.650
Aislinn-san...

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:04.180
She's drawing something?

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:09.900
What is that supposed to be?!

00:16:10.310 --> 00:16:13.710
"Let's enter the regional 
tournament and take first place."

00:16:13.710 --> 00:16:14.660
You understood that?!

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:15.980
Yes!

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:21.340
Well, let's have her sit down 
before we talk about the rules.

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:22.250
Yes!

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:23.920
So that means...

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:26.570
We've got our team.

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:29.090
One!

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:30.600
Two.

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:31.940
Three.

00:16:31.940 --> 00:16:32.550
Four.

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:34.960
Five.

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:38.590
M-Me?!

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:54.990
<i>Before then, I'd never 
left our mountain village.</i>

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:59.780
<i>The only enjoyment I had in life was the TV.</i>

00:17:00.510 --> 00:17:03.480
<i>But Kumakura-sensei brought me here,</i>

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:06.480
<i>and they all became my friends.</i>

00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:41.530
<i>The world I dreamed about back 
then has opened up to me here.</i>

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:56.480
<i>I want to keep going further and 
further, so I can't lose now!</i>

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:04.180
Bonus Hand 1!

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:33.340
Pon!

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:35.960
<i>Again?</i>

00:18:36.640 --> 00:18:39.050
<i>She's calling right from the beginning again.</i>

00:18:57.740 --> 00:18:58.900
Chi!

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:23.010
Chi!

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:24.510
Huh?

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:27.320
<i>She just discarded that 
tile on her last turn.</i>

00:19:27.320 --> 00:19:29.100
<i>Now she's calling it to get it back?</i>

00:19:29.990 --> 00:19:32.440
<i>Normally, that would be pointless.</i>

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:37.550
<i>So maybe it's the calling 
in itself that is the point.</i>

00:19:46.150 --> 00:19:47.120
Pon!

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:51.710
<i>Four calls... Another naked wait?</i>

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:54.150
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:58.300
It's not alone!

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:15.960
Tsumo!

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:19.270
2,700 from all.

00:20:23.350 --> 00:20:25.400
Himematsu has finally been dethroned!

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:29.290
Himematsu High School 
(South Osaka)
 3rd Year
 Suehara Kyouko

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:30.520
Miyamori Girls' is in the lead!

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:32.290
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
 3rd Year
 Anetai Toyone

00:20:33.760 --> 00:20:34.670
All right!

00:20:35.010 --> 00:20:36.850
Suehara-senpai...

00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:39.170
We're not too far from third, either.

00:20:39.850 --> 00:20:41.680
How will Kiyosumi and Eisui,

00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:43.170
in third and fourth place, respond to that?

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:45.980
Saki-san...

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:48.680
In this second half of 
the fifth players' match,

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:51.830
Miyamori's Anetai has won 
continuously since the start,

00:20:51.830 --> 00:20:53.680
making a big move for her team.

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:57.400
She's got a much more varied 
skill set than I imagined.

00:20:57.400 --> 00:21:00.150
More varied?

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:05.300
<i>Iwate... the team from Touno.</i>

00:21:05.300 --> 00:21:08.700
<i>I thought none of them would 
be scary except the Mayoiga girl,</i>

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:10.970
<i>but then their fourth player</i>

00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:14.210
<i>almost locked down Hatsumi-chan completely.</i>

00:21:16.310 --> 00:21:19.560
<i>Now this girl comes out of nowhere 
in the fifth players' match.</i>

00:21:20.080 --> 00:21:24.410
<i>Her team had quite the ace up their sleeve.</i>

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:29.750
<i>If you press into the mountains,
you will find a beautiful woman,</i>

00:21:30.370 --> 00:21:32.660
<i>a woman of tall growth,</i>

00:21:32.660 --> 00:21:36.810
<i>her unbound black hair even 
longer than her height.</i>

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:40.770
Bonus Hand 2!

00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:46.310
<i>Two naked waits in a row, and 
she won both hands with a tsumo!</i>

00:21:46.310 --> 00:21:51.290
<i>So she's got multiple skills... 
There might be more coming.</i>

00:21:52.590 --> 00:21:55.390
<i>Can I adjust for it in time?</i>

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:02.990
<i>I'm good at defense, but it looks 
like that won't work this time.</i>

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:07.550
<i>This is not my specialty,</i>

00:22:09.540 --> 00:22:11.480
<i>but I'll give it a try!</i>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>Next time:</b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>Threat</b>

00:23:36.870 --> 00:23:38.600
Sanma (3 player mahjong) 
is most enjoyed in

00:23:38.600 --> 00:23:40.350
the Kansai region, and there 
are lots of different rules.

00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:42.030
Nodoka-chan, you sure know a lot.

00:23:42.030 --> 00:23:43.550
I know a lot, too!

00:23:43.550 --> 00:23:45.770
For Tokyo's finest grilled 
sanma (mackerel pike), go to Meguro!

00:23:45.770 --> 00:23:48.070
In Tokyo, that would be Akasaka.

00:23:50.830 --> 00:23:55.920
<b>Watch Again!</b>
